course: dictionary
lesson: 15803
title: Unbalanced: not steady, not even
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unbalanced means not steady, or not even. Picture a chair with one short leg. It wobbles and may tip over, because its weight is not spread evenly.
explain: Use the words around it. «The table was unbalanced, so the glass kept sliding off.» The glass sliding off tells you the table was not steady.
explain: The word can also describe things that are not fair or even, such as «an unbalanced diet» with far too many sweets and not enough vegetables. Ask yourself: what is there too much of, and what is missing?
explain: In maths and science, unbalanced can mean that two sides are not equal, or that forces are not equal. Check the clues in the sentence, then swap in your meaning to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Unbalanced means not steady, likely to tip or fall because the weight is not spread evenly.
fact: «An unbalanced diet» has too much of some things and not enough of others, so it is not healthy.
fact: In science, unbalanced forces make things start moving, speed up or change direction.
fact: Balanced forces keep things steady.
fact: In maths, an unbalanced equation is not equal on both sides.
exercise: «The stool was unbalanced, so it wobbled when Sam sat on it.» What does unbalanced mean here? | Painted bright blue | *Not steady, likely to tip | Very tall and thin | Full of water
exercise: «Her diet was unbalanced: she ate only crisps and sweets.» What does unbalanced suggest? | Perfectly fair and even | *Too much of some things and not enough of others | Full of vegetables | Very cold
exercise: In science, what do unbalanced forces do to a still object? | Make it turn into water | Keep it perfectly still | Make it smaller | *Make it start moving
test: Which sentence uses unbalanced to mean not steady? | *«The tall bookcase was unbalanced and nearly tipped over.» | «Her unbalanced report was fair and even.» | «The unbalanced team was painted green.»
test: In maths, when is an equation unbalanced? | When both sides equal zero | *When the two sides are not equal | When the two sides are the same colour | When it has only one number
exam: Dev says «an unbalanced diet» is the healthiest kind. What is wrong with his idea? | It has exactly the right amount of everything | *It has too much of some things and not enough of others | Nothing is wrong with his idea | It means the food is cold
